Name every object as the autorelease pool drains.

A pool drain that faults inside objc_release says only that SOMETHING in the pool was already dead,
and by then that object's isa is unreadable, so the crash itself can never name it. The line printed
just BEFORE the fault can, because the object is still readable at that point.

That is the whole question for a daemon that dies parking its main thread: trustd checks in for its
service and then takes a SIGSEGV in AutoreleasePoolPage::releaseUntil, and nothing anywhere says
what it was releasing.

CIDER_TRACE_POOL, off unless asked for, one getenv the first time through.

VERIFIED SPEAKING on the happy path: with the gate on, a trustd run that does NOT crash prints

    CIDER_POOL releasing 0x786f6367c980 isa=0x786f64933168 __NSCFString

which is a normal drain of one object. An instrument has to be seen working before its silence can
be read as an answer.
--- a/runtime/NSObject.mm
+++ b/runtime/NSObject.mm
@@ -949,6 +949,33 @@
             page->protect();
 
             if (obj != POOL_BOUNDARY) {
+                /*
+                 * CIDER_TRACE_POOL: name every object as it leaves the pool.
+                 *
+                 * A drain that faults inside objc_release says only that SOMETHING in the pool was
+                 * already dead, and by then its isa is unreadable, so the crash itself can never
+                 * name it. The line printed just BEFORE the fault can: this prints the object and,
+                 * while it is still readable, its class.
+                 *
+                 * That is the whole question for a daemon that dies parking its main thread. It is
+                 * off unless asked for, and it costs a getenv once.
+                 */
+                {
+                    static int cider_pool_trace = -1;
+
+                    if (cider_pool_trace < 0) {
+                        const char *v = getenv("CIDER_TRACE_POOL");
+                        cider_pool_trace = (v != NULL && v[0] != '\0') ? 1 : 0;
+                    }
+                    if (cider_pool_trace) {
+                        Class cls = object_getClass(obj);
+                        const char *nm = cls ? class_getName(cls) : "(no class)";
+
+                        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_POOL releasing %p isa=%p %s\n",
+                                (void *) obj, (void *) cls, nm ? nm : "(unnamed)");
+                        fflush(stderr);
+                    }
+                }
 #if SUPPORT_AUTORELEASEPOOL_DEDUP_PTRS
                 // release count+1 times since it is count of the additional
                 // autoreleases beyond the first one
